-- title:
--   Two coefficient maps agree on Frᵈ-fixed elements up to Fr^j
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ (as a `Fact`) and a characteristic-zero commutative domain $\mathcal{O}$ together with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that the quotient $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$. Let $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero commutative domain which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, and assume: $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; that ideal is maximal; every $x \in \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $(\pi)$; every monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $(\pi)$; and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^{r} \in (\pi)$ for all $x$. Let $k$ be a field which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, let $\psi, \psi' : \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ be two $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphisms, and let $d$ be a nonzero integer. Then there is an integer $j$ such that $\psi'(y) = \psi(\mathrm{Fr}^{j} y)$ for every $y \in \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with $\mathrm{Fr}^{d} y = y$, the powers $\mathrm{Fr}^{d}$, $\mathrm{Fr}^{j}$ being taken in the group of $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphisms.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement that two $\mathcal{O}$-points of the completed unramified coefficient ring with values in a field of residue characteristic $r$ differ, on each finite Frobenius level $\{\,y : \mathrm{Fr}^{d} y = y\,\}$, by an integral power of Frobenius — the abstract form of the fact that two embeddings of a finite field into a field are conjugate under the Frobenius. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the identification of fibres of the fine family for the quaternionic moduli problem and in the criterion for two such fine-family points to coincide up to a level structure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_exists_forall_apply_eq_apply_frobenius_zpow_of_fixed.lean

